degrade their audience.

00:11:27.979 --> 00:11:31.090
It's so interesting to me
that a statement like that is

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.858
interpreted as a negative.

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:35.134
I actually think I'm helping.

00:11:35.134 --> 00:11:40.033
I'm trying to help the millions
of kids that have been sold on

00:11:40.033 --> 00:11:42.268
the propaganda that 
entrepreneurship is for

00:11:42.268 --> 00:11:44.571
everybody and they're not
deploying self-awareness

00:11:44.571 --> 00:11:46.506
to who they actually are.

00:11:46.506 --> 00:11:50.053
And so to me, just 'cause
you're getting critical feedback

00:11:50.053 --> 00:11:52.278
doesn't mean 
you're hurting somebody.

00:11:52.278 --> 00:11:56.703
Think we've gotten so soft in a
lot of arenas that even debating

00:11:56.703 --> 00:12:01.487
something that may not feel
warm and fuzzy is met with the

00:12:01.487 --> 00:12:03.556
thought that it's a negative.

00:12:03.556 --> 00:12:06.492
I can tell you right now that my
parents taught me a ton of shit

00:12:06.492 --> 00:12:08.464
that wasn't 
delivered with honey.

00:12:08.464 --> 00:12:12.465
And so, I think we need to
debate what teaching is really

00:12:12.465 --> 00:12:17.407
about and more importantly that
there are many delivery styles

00:12:17.407 --> 00:12:22.175
and ways to deliver a message
and not all of us react the same

00:12:22.175 --> 00:12:23.610
way to every one of them.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:27.180
And so, some people respond
extremely well to one way and

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.554
some respond to others and 
I think the earmark of trying to

00:12:30.554 --> 00:12:34.153
provide value is trying to
reach and communicate to many

00:12:34.153 --> 00:12:36.331
different people 
many different ways.

